{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKZ4L4seuiN6CTit6FWmVa","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c351867-3c9c-4124-beb4-0ae84097512a","uuid":"aeb463a0-9174-46e4-beef-44f2feeb4d90","timestamp":"2026-06-10T09:21:16.007Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **sos_257:** `ManaPool` models exactly one restriction kind","newString":"- **sos_13:** RULEBOOK 722.3c contradicts the TODO's \"cast for free\" — the\n  prepared copy is created in exile *when the permanent becomes prepared*\n  and is later cast normally (paying {W}). Implemented per the rulebook:\n  the activated-ability cost pays {W} (restricted instant/sorcery mana\n  allowed) and the effect casts via `cast_spell_free` (payment already\n  made). A one-shot replacement makes the resolved/countered copy cease to\n  exist instead of hitting a graveyard; it also ceases if Emeritus leaves\n  the battlefield. ETB clause runs in `on_resolve` (the fdn_205 reference\n  pattern), counting Emeritus itself in the \"more creatures than you\" check.\n- **sos_13:** the Inkling token's white/black color identity isn't modeled —\n  the engine has no color attribute for tokens (colors derive from mana\n  cost). Token is 1/1 flying Inkling, which is everything observable.\n- **sos_257:** `ManaPool` models exactly one restriction kind","originalFile":"# Key decisions log\n\n- **E1:** Fired `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` from `cast_spell_free` as well as\n  `cast_spell` — casting without paying the cost is still casting (rule 601),\n  so cast-watching abilities (e.g. Casualty, the sos_257 pump) must see free\n  casts. Copies pushed via `copy_spell` still fire nothing, as planned.\n- **sos_1:** The plan's replacement seam couldn't work as written — the engine\n  only consulted replacement effects for battlefield→graveyard moves, and\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was never fired. Added two additive engine edits:\n  fire attack triggers at the end of `declare_attackers_step`, and pass a new\n  `SpellPutIntoGraveyardReplacementEvent` from `_resolve_spell` (gate in\n  `move_to_zone` relaxed to \"whenever the caller supplies an event\").\n  Limitation (commented): a spell countered via a card-local `_counter_spell`\n  is added to the graveyard directly, bypassing the exile-instead replacement.\n- **sos_1:** \"may cast target …\" — with exactly one legal card the trigger\n  auto-selects it without prompting (per TODO); with several, `choose_card`\n  returning `None` declines.\n- **Ability activation in tests:** the workspace has no `ActivateAbility`\n  helper (despite the run instructions naming one); the engine's real\n  activation path is `engine.abilities.activate_ability` with an\n  `ActivatedAbilityInstance`/`LoyaltyAbilityInstance` built from the card's\n  printed ability list (by index). Tests use small local wrappers around\n  that path and resolve non-mana abilities off the stack via `resolve_top`.\n- **sos_57:** \"your next main phase\" is implemented as your next *precombat*\n  main (E2 only fires there, per the plan). If Mana Sculpt resolves during\n  your own turn before/during combat, a strict reading would let the mana\n  arrive at that turn's postcombat main; here it arrives at your next\n  precombat main instead. Deliberate plan-scoped simplification.\n- **sos_57:** added `card.mana_spent` (total paid; 0 for free casts) to the\n  casting pipeline, mirroring `colors_spent` — the engine recorded colors\n  but not the amount.\n- **sos_120:** the Paradigm copy uses `copy_spell` (per TODO), so it is a\n  stack copy rather than a \"cast\" — it can't be hit by cast triggers, and it\n  never touches a zone (a real copy ceases to exist anyway). Copies are\n  flagged `_is_paradigm_copy` so resolving one doesn't re-exile or register\n  a second recurring trigger (\"after you *first* resolve…\").\n- **sos_257:** `ManaPool` models exactly one restriction kind\n  (\"instant_or_sorcery\"), spent restricted-first within a mana type; the\n  pool's `total()`/`get()` stay unrestricted-only so FDN cards' cost checks\n  can't see unusable mana. The {5} animation is permanent, so it is baked\n  into `_original_card_types` rather than modeled as a continuous effect.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":6,"newStart":34,"newLines":18,"lines":["   never touches a zone (a real copy ceases to exist anyway). Copies are","   flagged `_is_paradigm_copy` so resolving one doesn't re-exile or register","   a second recurring trigger (\"after you *first* resolve…\").","+- **sos_13:** RULEBOOK 722.3c contradicts the TODO's \"cast for free\" — the","+  prepared copy is created in exile *when the permanent becomes prepared*","+  and is later cast normally (paying {W}). Implemented per the rulebook:","+  the activated-ability cost pays {W} (restricted instant/sorcery mana","+  allowed) and the effect casts via `cast_spell_free` (payment already","+  made). A one-shot replacement makes the resolved/countered copy cease to","+  exist instead of hitting a graveyard; it also ceases if Emeritus leaves","+  the battlefield. ETB clause runs in `on_resolve` (the fdn_205 reference","+  pattern), counting Emeritus itself in the \"more creatures than you\" check.","+- **sos_13:** the Inkling token's white/black color identity isn't modeled —","+  the engine has no color attribute for tokens (colors derive from mana","+  cost). Token is 1/1 flying Inkling, which is everything observable."," - **sos_257:** `ManaPool` models exactly one restriction kind","   (\"instant_or_sorcery\"), spent restricted-first within a mana type; the","   pool's `total()`/`get()` stay unrestricted-only so FDN cards' cost checks"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
