{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01W9VWrw8vKdtLvhvfeopJdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All ten cards are implemented and everything is committed. Final state:\n\n**Test results:** the full suite passes — 1,249 tests (1,145 engine regression tests with zero regressions from baseline, the FDN reference tests, and 59 new SOS tests). All ten `card_impl.py` files import cleanly, all 13 TODO checklist items are `[x]`, and the tree is clean with one commit per item.\n\n**Shared engine changes (small, additive):**\n- **E1** — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` now fires from `cast_spell` *and* `cast_spell_free` (free casts are still casts per rule 601); `copy_spell` copies correctly fire nothing.\n- **E2** — new `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent`, fired from `GameState.advance_phase` after `empty_mana_pools()`.\n- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` aggregates `spell_cost_reduction` hooks from the caster's battlefield permanents for instants/sorceries.\n- Additional gaps the cards genuinely needed: attack triggers actually fire (the event existed but `declare_attackers_step` never fired it), spells resolving off the stack consult replacement effects (`SpellPutIntoGraveyardReplacementEvent` — enables \"exile it instead\"), `card.mana_spent` stamped at cast, instant/sorcery-restricted mana in `ManaPool`, `game.rng` for deterministic coin flips, and `Player.skip_turns` honored in turn rotation.\n\n**Spec-over-plan deviations worth knowing (all logged in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`):**\n- **sos_13:** RULEBOOK 722.3c contradicts the TODO — the prepared Swords copy is created in exile *when the permanent becomes prepared* and casting it **pays {W}** (not free). The ETB clause runs in `on_resolve`, mirroring fdn_205, since the engine deliberately never self-fires a permanent's own ETB trigger.\n- **sos_57 / sos_120:** \"your next main phase\" / \"first main phases\" are precombat-main only (E2's scope, per the plan); logged as a deliberate simplification.\n- **sos_120:** Paradigm copies are flagged so a resolving copy doesn't re-register the recurring trigger or leave a phantom card in the graveyard.\n\nEach card was verified two ways: its committed `tests.py` (engine-driven via `test_utils`, `activate_ability`, `resolve_top`, `run_turn`), plus a throwaway smoke check per card asserting spec-observable outcomes I hadn't written tests for (e.g. retargeted casualty copies, restricted mana paying generic costs, animated land dying to lethal damage, miracle through the real turn loop, zero-heads ultimate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":307871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c351867-3c9c-4124-beb4-0ae84097512a","uuid":"80410611-e0d2-4a44-a137-bd94db39232b","request_id":"req_011CbuLooq16RFRWxyHMCYte"}
